 "lesson": {
  "slides": [
   {
    "id": "L1",
    "type": "num",
    "graph": "flat",
    "text": "An **area function** adds up area from a fixed start to a moving end.\n$$A(x) = int[0,x] 2 dt$$\nThe graph of $f(t) = 2$ is a flat line, so the area is a rectangle.",
    "answer": 6,
    "label": "$A(3)$ =",
    "hint": "The rectangle is 3 wide and 2 tall.",
    "explain": "Width 3 times height 2."
   },
   {
    "id": "L2",
    "type": "expr",
    "text": "$$A(x) = int[0,x] 2 dt$$\nNow let the right edge be $x$ instead of 3. The rectangle is $x$ wide and 2 tall.",
    "answer": "2x",
    "vars": [
     "x"
    ],
    "keys": [],
    "label": "$A(x)$ =",
    "show": "$2x$",
    "ranges": {
     "x": [
      0.3,
      1.2
     ]
    },
    "hint": "Width times height.",
    "explain": "$A(x) = 2x$."
   },
   {
    "id": "L3",
    "type": "mc",
    "text": "$A(x) = 2x$, so $A'(x) = 2$. Where have you seen that 2 before?",
    "options": [
     "It is the height of the function being integrated, $f(t) = 2$",
     "It is the left endpoint",
     "Nowhere. It is a coincidence"
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "hint": "Look inside the integral.",
    "explain": "The area grows at a rate equal to the height at the moving edge. That is the whole theorem."
   },
   {
    "id": "L4",
    "type": "expr",
    "text": "Try a slanted one. Under $f(t) = t$, the area from 0 to $x$ is a triangle, $x$ wide and $x$ tall.\n$$A(x) = int[0,x] t dt$$",
    "answer": "x^2/2",
    "vars": [
     "x"
    ],
    "keys": [],
    "label": "$A(x)$ =",
    "show": "$frac{x^2}{2}$",
    "ranges": {
     "x": [
      0.3,
      1.2
     ]
    },
    "graph": "tri",
    "hint": "Half of base times height.",
    "explain": "$A(x) = frac{x^2}{2}$, and its derivative is $x$: again the height of $f$ at the moving edge."
   },
   {
    "id": "L5",
    "type": "expr",
    "text": "**The Fundamental Theorem, Part 1.** It works for every continuous $f$:\n$$frac{d}{dx} int[a,x] f(t) dt = f(x)$$\nThe derivative of the area function is the function. Find\n$$frac{d}{dx} int[1,x] t^3 dt$$",
    "answer": "x^3",
    "vars": [
     "x"
    ],
    "keys": [
     "sin(",
     "cos(",
     "tan(",
     "sqrt(",
     "e^(",
     "ln("
    ],
    "label": "derivative =",
    "show": "$x^3$",
    "hint": "Put $x$ in for $t$.",
    "explain": "$x^3$"
   },
   {
    "id": "L6",
    "type": "expr",
    "text": "With the chain rule:\n$$frac{d}{dx} int[a,g(x)] f(t) dt = f(g(x))·g'(x)$$\nFind\n$$frac{d}{dx} int[0,x^2] sin(t) dt$$",
    "answer": "sin(x^2)(2x)",
    "vars": [
     "x"
    ],
    "keys": [
     "sin(",
     "cos(",
     "tan(",
     "sqrt(",
     "e^(",
     "ln("
    ],
    "label": "derivative =",
    "show": "$sin(x^2)(2x)$",
    "hint": "Put $x^2$ in for $t$, then multiply by the derivative of $x^2$.",
    "explain": "$sin(x^2)·2x$"
   }
  ]
 },
