     "id": "T1",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$$A(x) = int[2,x] f(t) dt$$\nWhat is $A(2)$?",
     "options": [
      "0",
      "$f(2)$",
      "2",
      "It depends on $f$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "hint": "How wide is the region from 2 to 2?",
     "explain": "No width, so no area."
    },
    {
     "id": "T2",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$$frac{d}{dx} int[1,x] cos(t^2) dt =$$",
     "options": [
      "$cos(x^2)$",
      "$-2x sin(x^2)$",
      "$cos(x^2) - cos(1)$",
      "$sin(x^2)$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "hint": "You do not need an antiderivative of $cos(t^2)$. (Nobody has a formula for one.)",
     "explain": "Part 1: the derivative of the area function is the integrand, with $x$ in place of $t$."
    },
    {
     "id": "T3",
     "type": "tf",
     "text": "Changing the lower limit from 1 to 5 changes the value of\n$$frac{d}{dx} int[1,x] f(t) dt$$",
     "answer": false,
     "hint": "What does moving the starting point do to the area function?",
     "explain": "A different start shifts the area by a constant, and the derivative of a constant is 0. The answer is $f(x)$ either way."
    },
    {
     "id": "T4",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$$frac{d}{dx} int[a,g(x)] f(t) dt =$$",
