      "$f(g(x))$",
      "$f(x)g'(x)$",
      "$F(g(x))$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "Part 1 plus the chain rule."
    },
    {
     "id": "T5",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$$frac{d}{dx} int[x,3] f(t) dt =$$",
     "options": [
      "$-f(x)$",
      "$f(x)$",
      "$f(3)$",
      "0"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "hint": "Part 1 needs $x$ on top. What does swapping the limits do?",
     "explain": "Swap the limits first: $int[x,3] f(t) dt = -int[3,x] f(t) dt$."
    },
    {
     "id": "T6",
     "type": "tf",
     "text": "Part 1 says that every continuous function has an antiderivative.",
     "answer": true,
     "hint": "What is the derivative of $A(x) = int[a,x] f(t) dt$?",
     "explain": "The area function $A(x) = int[a,x] f(t) dt$ is one: its derivative is $f(x)$."
    }
   ]
